.TH DEMAKE\-BUILD 1 "" "" "Build a Demotic game (.dmt) into a playable ROM"
.SH NAME
demake-build \- Build a Demotic game (.dmt) into a playable ROM
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdemake build\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIinput\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Build a Demotic game (.dmt) into a playable ROM.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI<n>\fR
Candidates to fit at once: a number, or auto for one per core. (default: auto)
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-console\fR \fI<id>\fR
Target console (a backend must exist; today: gb, gbc, nes, sms, gg, snes). (default: gb)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIvalue\fR
Output a playable ROM, or the symbol map for profiling. (default: rom)
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<text>\fR
Cartridge title (default: the source file's name).
.TP
\fB\-\-boot-logo\fR
Stamp the boot logo via rgbfix, so the ROM boots on real hardware.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<file>\fR
Write the artifact to <file> (default: stdout when piped).
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single JSON object on stdout (product goes to \-o).
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic detail (repeatable).
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress warnings.
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite an existing output file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
demake build pong.dmt \-o pong.gb
.br
a playable Game Boy cartridge
.PP
demake build pong.dmt \-\-title PONG \-\-json
.br
report what went in it
.PP
demake build pong.dmt \-\-format sym \-o pong.sym
.br
symbols, for a cycle profile
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBdemake\fR(1)
